## Persian. Every string here is lifted from the screen that already drew it —
## the `*Fa` mirrors — rather than translated afresh, so the fold cannot change
## a word the drawings settled.
##
## Persian has one plural form in CLDR's `other` sense for counted nouns: a
## noun after a number does not inflect (۱ سرویس and ۳ سرویس are both correct),
## which board 97's mirror recorded as the reason its count had no
## `if count == 1` branch. `nplurals=2` is still declared because Gettext
## requires the header and CLDR gives fa two categories (one, other); the
## `one` form is simply the same word.
msgid ""
msgstr ""
"Language: fa\n"
"Plural-Forms: nplurals=2; plural=(n > 1);\n"

